# Umami analytics
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID is baked into the image at BUILD time, not read
# at run time. It is a Docker build ARG (docker/Dockerfile) and Next.js inlines
# every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value into the client bundle during `pnpm build`, so
# setting it in the environment of an already built container changes nothing.
# Set it here before the image is built, and rebuild whenever it changes.
#
# On a fresh Umami this is a two pass deploy. Umami cannot mint a website id
# until it is serving, and it cannot serve until the stack is up, so the first
# build ships with this empty and the second build, after the site has been
# created in the Umami UI, is the one that actually measures anything. Skipping
# the second pass leaves a site that looks healthy and records no page views.
NEXT_PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_UMAMI_URL='https://analytics.cuatro.dev'

# Postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-in-prod.

# Umami App Secret (gnerate with: openssl rand -hex 32)
UMAMI_APP_SECRET=change-me-in-prod.

# Identity (Story 5.2): the one Clerk issuer and one OIDC client per application.
# Names derive from the Registry id (AD-3); values live only in GitHub Actions
# secrets and the on-box env files, never here. See ops/identity-issuer.md.
OIDC_ISSUER=
CUATRO_PORTFOLIO_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
CUATRO_PORTFOLIO_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
CS_TRACKER_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
CS_TRACKER_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
